{"name":"Windsor","hex":"#462c77","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Windsor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A market town in the Royal Borough of Windsor and Maidenhead, Berkshire, England, famous for Windsor Castle. See  Windsor, Berkshire on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia","Other places in England, besides the famous Windsor in Berkshire:\nA hamlet in Polperro parish, Cornwall .\nA neighbourhood of Crowle, North Lincolnshire district, Lincolnshire ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Windsor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Detroit–Windsor","blocks":[{"text":"The Detroit–Windsor region is an international transborder agglomeration named for the American city of Detroit, Michigan, the Canadian city of Windsor, Ontario, and the Detroit River, which separates them. The Detroit–Windsor area acts as a critical commercial link straddling the Canada–United States border and has a total population of 5,976,595. It is the largest cross-border conurbation in the western hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Detroit_and_Windsor_skylines_from_Belle_Isle_2025-09-07.jpg/330px-Detroit_and_Windsor_skylines_from_Belle_Isle_2025-09-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detroit%E2%80%93Windsor","wikidata":"Q5266069"},{"title":"Windsor, New South Wales","blocks":[{"text":"Windsor is a historic town in north-western Sydney in New South Wales, Australia. It is the council seat of the Hawkesbury local government area. The town sits on the Hawkesbury River, enveloped by farmland and Australian bush. Many of the oldest surviving European buildings in Australia are located at Windsor. It is 56 km (35 mi) north-west of the Sydney CBD, on the fringes of the city's urban sprawl."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/WindsorNSW.jpg/330px-WindsorNSW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windsor%2C_New_South_Wales","wikidata":"Q1026964"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Ouelletteave.jpg/500px-Ouelletteave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Ouelletteave.jpg/500px-Ouelletteave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View from Ouellette Avenue in Windsor to the north across the river to Detroit's Guardian (right) and Penobscot Building (left) cityscape.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOuelletteave.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/CasinoWindsorsignage.jpg/500px-CasinoWindsorsignage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/CasinoWindsorsignage.jpg/1280px-CasinoWindsorsignage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/CasinoWindsorsignage.jpg/500px-CasinoWindsorsignage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Casino Windsor (now Caesars Windsor) was a major contributing factor to Detroit's legalization of casino gaming.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACasinoWindsorsignage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/WindsorNSWChurch.JPG/500px-WindsorNSWChurch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/WindsorNSWChurch.JPG/500px-WindsorNSWChurch.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Sanctum at Sunny Brae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindsorNSWChurch.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Windso